  Name: "Stainless 304"
  Description: >-
    SAE 304 austenitic stainless steel (UNS S30400, DIN/EN 1.4301,
    EN X5CrNi18-10), annealed condition. One of the most common general-purpose
    stainless steels.
    Density, Young's modulus, Poisson's ratio, tensile/yield strength,
    specific heat, elongation: Wikipedia article "SAE 304 stainless steel"
    (CC-BY-SA-4.0), accessed 2026-04.
    Thermal conductivity and thermal expansion: typical values for 300-series
    austenitic stainless steel (widely-published engineering data).
    Machinability data derived from FreeCAD core 'AusteniticStainlessSteel.FCMat'
    (Jonas Bähr, CC-BY-3.0, sourced from Tabellenbuch Zerspantechnik
    ISBN 978-3-7585-1315-2). The Jonas prototype is generic austenitic
    stainless; 304 sits near the centre of that class so the prototype values
    are a reasonable match. Annealed 304 work-hardens aggressively; sharp
    tools and rigid setups improve actual results substantially over the
    conservative defaults shown here.
  SourceURL: "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SAE_304_stainless_steel"
